---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Meter from '../components/Meter.astro';
import Search from '../components/Search.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import { getHot, usd, ago, type Burst, type HotNow } from '../lib/api';

const hours = Number(Astro.url.searchParams.get('hours') ?? 24);
const feed = await getHot(hours);
const now: HotNow[] = feed?.now ?? [];
const recent: Burst[] = feed?.recent ?? [];
const hottest = Math.max(1, ...now.map((h) => h.conviction), ...recent.map((b) => b.conviction));

/** Old enough to have done something, and with a fill to measure it by. */
const judged = recent.filter((b) => b.age_at_read_h >= 3 && b.best !== null && !b.seeded);
const reached2x = judged.filter((b) => (b.best ?? 0) >= 2).length;
const belowHalf = judged.filter((b) => (b.last ?? 1) < 0.5).length;
const medianBest = judged.length
  ? [...judged].map((b) => b.best as number).sort((a, b) => a - b)[Math.floor(judged.length / 2)]
  : null;

const minutes = (b: { window_s: number }) => Math.max(1, Math.round(b.window_s / 60));
const ageText = (s: number | null) =>
  s === null ? '—' : s < 5400 ? `${Math.round(s / 60)} min old` : `${(s / 3600).toFixed(1)}h old`;
const x = (v: number | null) => (v === null ? '—' : `${v.toFixed(1)}×`);
const tone = (v: number | null) => (v === null ? 'm' : v >= 2 ? 'g' : v < 0.5 ? 'c' : '');
---
<Base
  title="Bursts — where several trusted Robinhood Chain wallets went in at once"
  description="Tokens that three or more trusted fomo.family wallets entered inside half an hour, caught within twenty seconds of the fill, with what the price did afterwards. The fast edge of the signal feed, and its own scorecard."
  section="bursts"
>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,5vw,44px)">Bursts</h1>
    <span class="badge" style="color:var(--amber)">{now.length} now</span>
  </div>
  <p class="verdict" style="margin-bottom:20px">
    The signal feed asks who the cohort is in over a day. This asks a narrower question: did the
    conviction arrive <b>all at once</b>? A burst requires at least {feed?.delta ?? 4} conviction,
    calculated as the sum of (score/100)², from at least {feed?.min_wallets ?? 3} trusted wallets.
    Each wallet must make its first observed buy inside the last {feed?.window_min ?? 30} minutes.
    The watcher targets twenty-second polling; source delays can make updates slower.
  </p>

  <dl class="strip">
    <div><dt>Bursting now</dt><dd class="a">{now.length}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Last {hours}h</dt><dd>{recent.length}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Old enough to judge</dt><dd>{judged.length}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Reached 2×</dt><dd class="g">{judged.length ? reached2x : '—'}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Ended below ½</dt><dd class="c">{judged.length ? belowHalf : '—'}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Median best</dt><dd>{x(medianBest)}</dd></div>
  </dl>

  {!feed && <p class="empty">The data service is not answering.</p>}

  {feed && now.length === 0 && (
    <p class="note">
      <b>No token currently meets the burst rule.</b> Both the conviction threshold and the
      minimum number of first buyers must be met inside the configured window.
      The list below contains recorded past bursts.
    </p>
  )}

  {now.length > 0 && (
    <Panel title="Bursting now" meta={`window ${feed?.window_min} min`}>
      <ul class="signals">
        {now.map((h, i) => (
          <li>
            <span class="rank">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <a class="tk" href={`/token/${h.mint}`}>${h.sym}</a>
            <span class="cv">+{h.conviction.toFixed(1)}</span>
            <Meter value={h.conviction} max={hottest} />
            <p class="who">
              <span class="a">{h.wallets} in over {Math.max(1, Math.round((h.last_ts - h.first_ts) / 60))} min</span>
              {' · '}{ageText(h.age_s)}{' · '}{usd(h.usd)}{' · '}
              {h.who.slice(0, 5).map((w, n) => (
                <><a href={`/trader/${w}`}>{w}</a> {h.scores[n]}{n < Math.min(4, h.who.length - 1) ? ' · ' : ''}</>
              ))}{h.who.length > 5 ? ` +${h.who.length - 5}` : ''}
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Panel>
  )}

  {recent.length > 0 && (
    <section style="margin-top:var(--section)">
      <h2 class="h2">Last {hours} hours <span class="m mono" style="font-weight:400;font-size:12px">· multiples of the price the last entrant paid</span></h2>
      <div class="tablewrap">
        <table class="bursts mono">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>when</th><th>token</th><th class="r">burst</th><th>wallets</th>
              <th class="r">age then</th><th class="r">best</th><th class="r">last fill</th><th class="r" title="the token's last stored quote, refreshed every fifteen minutes">quote</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {recent.map((b) => (
              <tr class={b.seeded ? 'seeded' : ''}>
                <td class="m">{ago(b.ts)} ago</td>
                <td><a class="tk" href={`/token/${b.mint}`}>${b.sym}</a>{b.seeded && <span class="badge flag" style="margin-left:8px" title="pushed into the wallets rather than bought by them; not counted">seeded</span>}</td>
                <td class="r a">+{b.conviction.toFixed(1)} <span class="m">/ {minutes(b)}m</span></td>
                <td class="m">{b.wallets} · {b.who.slice(0, 3).join(' · ')}{b.who.length > 3 ? ` +${b.who.length - 3}` : ''}</td>
                <td class="r m">{b.age_s === null ? '—' : b.age_s < 5400 ? `${Math.round(b.age_s / 60)}m` : `${(b.age_s / 3600).toFixed(1)}h`}</td>
                <td class={`r ${tone(b.best)}`}>{x(b.best)}</td>
                <td class={`r ${tone(b.last)}`}>{x(b.last)}</td>
                <td class={`r ${tone(b.now)}`}>{x(b.now)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <p class="note" style="margin-top:var(--section)">
    <b>What the replay said before this page existed.</b> Over 36 days of tape the same rule fired
    about five times a day; 39% of those reached 2× inside a day and about 40% ended the day
    below half, against 36% and 43% for the ordinary signal feed, which fires fifty times a day.
    Better on every measure and ten times quieter, and still a coin with a long tail: the value
    is in the best price, not in holding to the close. The scorecard above is that replay,
    continued live.
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top:var(--section)"><Search /></div>
</Base>

<style>
  .h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bursts { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bursts th, .bursts td { padding: 9px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--carbon); text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; }
  .bursts th { font-weight: 400; font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--graphite); }
  .bursts .r { text-align: right; }
  .bursts tr.seeded td { color: var(--carbon); text-decoration: line-through; }
  .bursts tr.seeded td .badge { text-decoration: none; }
  .bursts .tk { color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }
  .bursts .tk:hover { color: var(--amber); }
  .who a { color: var(--graphite); }
  .who a:hover { color: var(--amber); }
</style>
